I'm in love with Ivern Support - give me tips on my build please!
&amp;#x200B;

[That is ALL support games \(not ranked\)](https://i.redd.it/vsga0t1a0jq21.png)

&amp;#x200B;

I've been playing Ivern Support the last couple days and basically am addicted, it's so much fun! While the very early game can be a challenge sometimes &amp; you aren't capable of carrying as well the utility &amp; benefit that can be brought to the team mid/late game is amazing. Since this is the Ivern Main page I thought some of you more experienced players can give me some advice or make suggestions on how to optimize my runes/items/spells. I'm not really looking to take this to ranked anytime soon but I would like to make it as strong a build as possible. I'll put my questions in bold.

&amp;#x200B;

# My Runes

Summon Aery - **The Aery shield often seems like overkill and goes unused before the shield expires, should I replace with arcane comet?** 

Nullifying Orb

Celerity

Gathering Storm

&amp;#x200B;

Bone Plating 

Revitalize

&amp;#x200B;

Offense/Flex Adaptive/Defense HP

&amp;#x200B;

# My Normal Build Path

1. Nomads Medallion - I found that it's to difficult to proc spelltheif to make it worth it and the income from coin makes a much bigger impact overall. 
2. Boots of Mobility
3. Ardent Censer
4. Redemption
5. Unholy Grail
6. Deathcap
7. Open (What I take depends on the match-up but rarely get full build).

**Any suggestions on items I should take instead or if I should change the order I get these items ?**

&amp;#x200B;

&amp;#x200B;

&amp;#x200B;

**Finally, I take Ignite + Flash for my spells. I have thought about taking smite so I can steal enemy buffs but I am not sure about that. What do you guys think?**

&amp;#x200B;

&amp;#x200B;

**Thanks for the feedback!**

&amp;#x200B;

I have no doubt that Ivern is a better jungler and when I do jungle I play him, however I honestly find playing jungle quite boring. Just not my thing. I have an A with him as jungle and I'm pretty sure he's probably my highest winrate. When I play him I feel like I have a little more control over the outcome of the match as opposed to playing Warwick/Rengar (my other two) where my influence is somewhat more limited. 

&amp;#x200B;

I enjoy support though because I don't have to deal with CS which can be stressful &amp; I really like the gratitude when I'm able to get that perfect shield/stun and secure a kill or save a teammate. I really enjoy Iverns kit so much that I can't resist taking him support :P

&amp;#x200B;

I am in low elo so that might be why I'm able to pull it off with a good win-rate. Levels 1-5 are pretty rough and we have to generally tower-camp but once I hit 6 we usually dominate lane and it's rare that I lose first tower as Ivern support or get killed during the laning phase. 

&amp;#x200B;

&amp;#x200B;

HAH I see that you mentioned Unsealed Spellbook! That is quite funny because I just mentioned to the other person that I had the idea to try that. Now that you have pointed it out I will REALLY try it. I don't think I'd take Smite as my primary though just because people on my team would freak out &amp; I'd rather not deal with it. Would probably take ignite &amp; then just switch to smite when the enemy buff was available.   


But yeah no question that Morgana is a superior support I mean, when I play her I straight dominate and often will get more kills than my ADC (unintentionally) because I just go so hard with her but I like Ivern because he's a bit of a challenge but is capable of some really impressive game-swinging plays. 

&amp;#x200B;

I have a similar spiritual belief however mine really began when I had a near-death experience. Really it's difficult to put into words what I believe but this is how I explain it to most people.

&amp;#x200B;

&amp;#x200B;

Imagine if the universe itself is a diamond. A diamond has many edges that all cast a unique reflection. As time passes imagine the diamond moving - the reflections move, some vanish and some new appear.

&amp;#x200B;

Now imagine if our human consciousness &amp; the consciousness of higher beings (animals) are those reflections. We are unaware of the diamond itself and are only aware of our own reflection and those around us. Only when we are able to take our eyes off of our own reflection can we see and experience being the diamond. This is what most refer to as "ego loss".

&amp;#x200B;

So there is an ultimate universal consciousness - I don't mean conscious in the human sense but the universe itself is sentient. The universe is constantly creating new reflections which are merely reflections of itself with various levels of consciousness. Why? I have no idea, perhaps this is how the universe experiences itself.

&amp;#x200B;

What I do know is that -

&amp;#x200B;

1. We all have the ability to view the universe from the perspective of that universal consciousness once we obtain ego loss - this can be with some psychedelic drugs such as DMT, near death experiences or even deep meditation.
2. We all come from the same source &amp; we are all OF the same source. Everyone is connected because we are all just a reflection of the same source. When we die we all experience existence in the exact same way as the universal consciousness.
3. At the same time every being capable of consciousness has a unique specific consciousness such as human, animal, etc. that is unique for that specific reflection.
4. We should treat nature &amp; other beings with the utmost respect because we are all from the same source. We don't know why we are created or what the purpose for each reflection may be - perhaps when we die we will "know" why we lived or what our purpose was.
5. Time works differently in the universe. Our entire idea of time is not a concrete law but one that applies because of various rules given on our physical world. You only need to read about black holes to understand that time can be nonexistent. For example at the deepest point in a black hole (singularity) it's been highly theorized that time would no longer exist. You would be able to see everything that had been in the black hole in the past and everything that was coming into the black hole in the future.  Thus the universe has no concept of time. Imagine if our idea of time is a straight line. The universe would be taking that line and instead making it a single point or even better imagine if the line was totally erased but the universe still existed.

&amp;#x200B;

&amp;#x200B;

This is what I believe because it's the only thing that I have experienced which has any TRUE sign of credibility. I've experienced it and maybe it was a hallucination in my head, maybe not but it's the realest I've got from any religion.

&amp;#x200B;

Feel free to ask me any more questions.

