Instantly ending the game as Heimer ADC Quadra-Kill
So this game we were probably going to win anyway since we had an inhibitor. They did manage to kill all of us at the dragon pit (after we got Infernal). Once we all died they made a mad dash to the Baron pit which was pretty obvious and I called out in chat. Luckily I had TP, ult &amp; Zonyas and that was all that I needed to get the Quadra kill. Meanwhile Lee was going to work on their nexus turrets, I assume they hoped that they could get baron &amp; then rush back &amp; kill Lee. Big mistake.

&amp;#x200B;

Never underestimate a Heimer with Zonyas &amp; never stick around at the Baron with your health that low!

&amp;#x200B;

**Best part? This was my 3rd promo game and I needed this win to rank up!**

https://reddit.com/link/bcl4xo/video/lekmue80jxr21/player

&amp;#x200B;

[Final Stats](https://i.redd.it/3eig1zfrjxr21.png)

Well I play Heimer as ADC so my opinions are based on that. The only three champions that pose a significant challenge to me are Miss Fortune, Morgana and Zyra. As for Miss Fortune &amp; Morgana they have a strong AOE ability that they can cast from far away (especially MF) that can easily shred my turrets over a wide area. Zyra is just strong AF because her plants &amp; the fact that she can put pressure on me from far away. I always ban MF and my duo partner always bands Zyra. 

&amp;#x200B;

As far as other lanes I imagine the biggest threat would be those champions that have the ranged ability to deal with your turrets or the burst ability to quickly jump in and kill you (like Zed). That's why I always ban Zed on midlane. 

&amp;#x200B;

&amp;#x200B;

Vayne you shouldn't have any issues with. Don't stand close to surfaces that she can stun you into. Same goes for Irelia. Save your E so you can punish her for going after your turrets. 

&amp;#x200B;

As far as Yasou goes he also is easy, just don't stay in the lane if your down past 50% health. He can all in you at that point so it's just not worth it. Hopefully if you play safe and are aware of when his next tornado comes you can dodge it. As long as you stay by your turrets the movement speed helps.

&amp;#x200B;

For Xerath it's pretty easy. Just farm away and look for good opportunities to poke him. He's squishy and will be heavily punished if he comes near your turrets.

&amp;#x200B;

&amp;#x200B;

Lastly one mistake I see a lot of players make is ulting their W or Q. In almost all situations where it's a 1 v 1 in the laning phase it's better to ult your E then follow up with a W and dropping turrets if necessary. The reason is that it's very easy to hit with your ult E, it stuns them &amp; also sets you up to guarantee a W hit. 

&amp;#x200B;

The exception is when your getting tower dived on (dropping a Q and then using Zonyas can work), if your trying to quickly destroy a tower (ulting Q can be good) or if your very confident that an ult W will hit.

The two strongest points for Heimer to me are his ability to rain hell down on objectives. Nothing can turn a fight more than dropping 2 turrets, ult Q your 3rd turret, follow with an E then Zonyas (especially if you have Ludens &amp; Deathcap). 

&amp;#x200B;

Same goes for Baron. I posted a quadra kill I got the other day where I just walked over to the enemy team who were fighting baron and dropped my turrets, ult Q and then Zonyas.

I actually used to main Zyra for a while. I got M7 but after playing Heimer she just feels like a frustrating and annoying version of him. The fact that her plants are so widely unpredictable makes her so annoying to play compared to Heimers deadly turrets. 

&amp;#x200B;

I'd say Illaoi is a lot closer because the general strategy in close fights is the same. With heimer you drop turrets and Zonyas if you get jumped on and with Illaoi you spawn a mass of tentacles around you then hope to hell you can heal yourself enough to survive before they die. Generally the same strategy.

My problem with Xerath is that if you have a bad laning phase or don't get fed your rendered basically useless to the team. Your Q and W will do little damage &amp; your ult even will hardly hurt them. Sure you have a stun but it's fairly slow &amp; doesn't last all that long. 

&amp;#x200B;

Heimer on the other hand can be relevant even when behind as his ult + e can be a massive turn in a team fight (being able to stun the entire team) and the fact he can drop turrets &amp; zonyas if he gets jumped on compared to Xerath who has to hope he can hit his E and that it will be enough for him to either secure the kill or get away. 

&amp;#x200B;

They aren't at all similar to me but maybe it's because I just hated Xerath.

How the hell do I beat the tourist islands mission?
I really wanted to avoid asking for advice but I can't help it. I've tried this mission 6 times at least. I've tried so many different strategies &amp; all seem to fail miserably such as:

1. Going straight tourist. Building no new industry and jumping straight into tourist objectives. I go bankrupt quickly and never recover.
2. Building lots of log cutting &amp; ship yards. This works for a time and I'm swimming in money yet I will find myself bankrupt as soon as I start working on the tourist area.
3. Building lots of Rum. This also led to bankruptcy once I started expanding onto the islands.
4. Building a small amount of shipyards &amp; rum and then going tourist.

&amp;#x200B;

Every scenario I fail. I had one where I was invaded &amp; had no defense so I watched helplessly as my entire tourist district was destroyed and then rage quit that play-through.

&amp;#x200B;

Another scenario I used nuclear testing to bank roll offshore oil drilling (all 4 of them) and for a time I made loads of cash. Sadly my population didn't forgive me &amp; my approval rating at one point was 0%. I gave up after people started burning all my buildings.

&amp;#x200B;

&amp;#x200B;

I had no issues with the first 3 missions I did so is this one just really hard or am I going about it the wrong way? Any help is appreciated!

&amp;#x200B;

&amp;#x200B;

[Coming along well!](https://i.redd.it/l4w6wyfmr9t21.png)

Same here. I think that I must have tried this at least 10 times and probably spent 20+ hours.

&amp;#x200B;

I finally followed the tips here and just focused on mining &amp; boats. (no logging). I managed to get over a million in the bank then I started the tourism part. For that I basically created "tourist centers" on the big islands each featured one of the landmarks in the middle. This created a big draw to the area.  


One tip I can give you is that once you start on the tourism part don't rush it. Take your time crafting each island carefully. Try to create an island featured around our tourist type such as "Thrill Seeking" but also have an attraction or two for other guests. The good thing about the landmarks is that everyone loves them so even if there is no other attractions for a guest they have that to increase happiness.

&amp;#x200B;

The hardest part is getting the 70/70 happiness - for this I just watched the heat map and tried to increase happiness where I saw red. Sometimes this means unchecking "tourists only" and sometimes it meant building new attractions if I can see the building was red because for example it contained cultural tourists but there was no cultural attractions nearby.

